WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.560
Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim.

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.010
We've reached now,

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:05.530
we had MAR SHES,

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:09.050
which is I recognize that
everyone has been my mom.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.080
And then DRIN DRAN,

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.460
I think about all the good
things they did for me

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.110
when they were my mom,

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.727
even the ant crawling across
the floor of the bathroom.

00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:19.560
DRIN GZO

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.270
We just had to pay her back

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:24.760
with more than she gave you.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.380
Give her Buddhahood

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.830
in exchange for bringing you up.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:30.882
Now we've reached the
fourth step which is called

00:00:30.882 --> 00:00:32.054
YID 'ONG BYAMS PA

00:00:32.054 --> 00:00:34.120
YID 'ONG BYAMS PA

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.400
You guys all know the word BYAMS PA

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.809
It's like Maitri, my grandson's name.

00:00:40.809 --> 00:00:44.420
But YID 'ONG means beautiful.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.660
They look beautiful to you.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:50.929
The people look beautiful to
you and you feel love for them.

00:00:50.929 --> 00:00:54.504
So we're going to cover
now the fourth part.

00:00:54.504 --> 00:00:57.880
BZHI PA YID 'ONG GI BYAMS PA BSGOM PA LA

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.590
That's the next line.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:03.215
Let's read the next paragraph.

00:01:03.215 --> 00:01:05.147
DE'I RNAM PA NI SEMS CAN RNAMS

00:01:05.147 --> 00:01:07.697
SNYING DU SDUG CING GCES LA PHANGS PA'I

00:01:07.697 --> 00:01:10.980
RNAM PAR 'CHAR BA ZHIG STE

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:15.810
You reach this fourth level
when you look at people

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:20.810
and you feel like they look
super beautiful to you.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.350
Like you're just around normal people,

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.653
and you're just doing
normal things with them,

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:30.107
and then you just look
at them and you're like,

00:01:30.107 --> 00:01:32.535
"Man, they're so beautiful."

00:01:32.535 --> 00:01:35.230
Not necessarily physically, right?

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:39.930
But you feel this beauty
in the people around you.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:42.300
It's kind of like when
you're working together

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.370
with a bunch of people.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:47.686
You do some hard work together,
and you get the work done,

00:01:47.686 --> 00:01:50.911
and then everyone looks beautiful to you.

00:01:50.911 --> 00:01:53.856
RNAM PAR 'CHAR BA means
that's how it looks to you.

00:01:53.856 --> 00:01:56.980
DGE BSHES PO TO BAS AA MA RGAN MO ZHIG LA

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.720
So DGE BSHES PO TO BAS was
one of those Kadampa lamas

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.520
about a thousand years ago in Tibet.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.460
And one older woman,

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:07.451
AA MA RGAN MO

00:02:07.451 --> 00:02:08.618
means older woman,

00:02:08.618 --> 00:02:13.615
came up to him, and she said,
"What is this beautiful love?"

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.070
What does it mean to have that love

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:22.356
where you see the people
around you as really beautiful?

00:02:22.356 --> 00:02:24.554
What is that?

00:02:24.554 --> 00:02:26.590
How do you describe that?
How do you get that?

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:27.423
And he said,

00:02:27.423 --> 00:02:31.015
KHYOD KYI BU THOD LE
KOR LA JI LTAR BYAMS PA

00:02:31.015 --> 00:02:34.030
It's the kind of love that
you have for your son.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:37.390
Her son's name was THOD LE KOR.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:42.200
So it's like John, or Pachi, or something.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:46.414
He says that the love you
have for your son, Pachi,

00:02:46.414 --> 00:02:48.690
that's beautiful love.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.103
And the goal is to have it for everybody.

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:55.484
You see him as super beautiful
because he is your son.

00:02:55.484 --> 00:02:58.821
But now can you have that for everybody?

00:02:58.821 --> 00:03:01.946
BYAMS PA NI KHYOD KYI BU THOD
LE KOR LA JI LTAR BYAMS PA

00:03:01.946 --> 00:03:05.446
DE LTAR YIN GSUNGS PA
LTAR SEMS CAN THAMS CAD BU

00:03:05.446 --> 00:03:07.445
YID DU 'ONG BA DANG 'DRA BAR

00:03:07.445 --> 00:03:11.052
When you see all the people
around you as very beautiful,

00:03:11.052 --> 00:03:12.916
they strike you as very beautiful.

00:03:12.916 --> 00:03:15.783
MTHONG BA LA YID 'ONG GI BYAMS PA

00:03:15.783 --> 00:03:19.020
That's what we call step number four

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:21.561
in developing bodhisattva's vision,

00:03:21.561 --> 00:03:24.728
bohichitta, is called beautiful love.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:28.610
Sees people as beautiful.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:32.930
We have that picture of
the mom with her child.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.100
You can imagine

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:37.428
that she sees her child very beautiful.

00:03:37.428 --> 00:03:40.044
She has a crush on her baby.

00:03:40.044 --> 00:03:42.740
She sees him as very, very beautiful.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:45.397
All right, let's go back to the text.

00:03:45.397 --> 00:03:47.422
'DI LA DMIGS PA LOGS SU MI DGOS PAR

00:03:47.422 --> 00:03:49.180
Now a very interesting idea.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:51.440
He says, "By the way,

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:54.630
you don't need to study step number four."

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:57.580
You don't need to study step number four.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:00.650
Then you like, "What? I'm
studying it right now."

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.350
He says, "No, you don't need to study it."

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:06.400
Recognize that people
have been your mother.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.210
Think about the kindness they showed you.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.550
Think about paying back the kindness

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.520
and then automatically,

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.570
we can see a picture here,

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:20.380
You're on a auto pilot, right?

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:22.870
You don't have to steer the car.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:27.870
Your mind will go directly
to seeing her as beautiful.

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:31.860
Once you decide that you
would like to push her,

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.730
your mom into enlightenment,

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:35.630
of course, you're going
to see her as beautiful.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:37.820
So Pabongka Rinpoche says,

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:39.810
step number four is kind of automatic.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:42.200
If you do the first three steps,

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:45.630
then the fourth step is going
to come up just automatically.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.717
You don't have to think about it.

00:04:47.717 --> 00:04:51.367
'DI LA DMIGS PA LOGS SU MI
DGOS PAR GONG GI MAR SHES

00:04:51.367 --> 00:04:56.329
DRIN DRAN DRIN GZO GSUM
LA SNGON DU MYONG BA THON

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.689
MYONG BA THON means get good at them.

00:04:58.689 --> 00:05:01.380
If you get good at the first three steps:

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:04.240
see them as your mom, think
about what they did for you,

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.012
want to pay them back;

00:05:06.012 --> 00:05:07.487
RANG SHUGS KYIS 'BYUNG BA

00:05:07.487 --> 00:05:08.862
RANG SHUGS KYIS means

00:05:08.862 --> 00:05:11.062
means it's just going
to happen automatically.

00:05:11.062 --> 00:05:15.087
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD KYI
RGYUD LA ZAG MED KYI BDE BA

00:05:15.087 --> 00:05:19.212
LTA GA LA YOD DE ZAG BCAS
KYI BDE BA TZAM YANG MI 'DUG

00:05:19.212 --> 00:05:24.212
But what's the current
state of all beings?

00:05:24.439 --> 00:05:25.272
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD

00:05:25.272 --> 00:05:29.428
What's going on with all
the people in the universe?

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:31.261
ZAG MED KYI BDE BA LTA GA LA

00:05:31.261 --> 00:05:36.260
LTA GA LA YOD DE means forget it.

00:05:38.765 --> 00:05:42.890
They don't have ultimate
happiness in their hearts.

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:44.040
Forget it.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:46.540
They don't even have normal
happiness in their hearts.

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.620
They can't get even normal happiness.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:52.550
We're supposed to be paying our mom back

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:54.950
by taking her to ultimate happiness.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:59.950
But right now we can't even
give her regular happiness, even

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:04.803
for a few minutes difficult
to make another person happy.

00:06:06.118 --> 00:06:09.059
DA LTA KHO RANG TSOS BDE BAR RLOM PA

00:06:09.059 --> 00:06:12.120
DE YANG SDUG BSNGAL GYI
RANG BZHIN LAS MA 'DAS PAS

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:15.490
No, no, Geshe-la, my
mom is happy sometimes.

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:17.280
I'm also happy sometimes.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:21.143
That's just suffering in another suit.

00:06:22.844 --> 00:06:26.255
No, no, I have some
happy moments in my life.

00:06:26.255 --> 00:06:29.750
It's just suffering with sugar on top.

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:32.107
It's just another kind of suffering.

00:06:32.107 --> 00:06:35.050
Most of the things you think are happiness

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:39.223
are really just pain with
a little sugar on top.

00:06:39.223 --> 00:06:41.289
DA NI SEMS CAN THAMS CAD
BDE BA THAMS CAD DANG

00:06:41.289 --> 00:06:43.415
LDAN NA CI MA RUNG

00:06:43.415 --> 00:06:47.800
You can talk about trying
to make all people,

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.340
give them ultimate happy,

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:52.400
give them all the happiness they can want.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:53.233
CI MA RUNG

00:06:53.233 --> 00:06:54.999
Yeah, that would be nice.

00:06:54.999 --> 00:06:56.250
CI MA RUN

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:57.421
And by the way,

00:06:57.421 --> 00:07:02.421
here we get into our kind
of Tibetan philosophy,

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:05.961
which is very close to
the Four Immeasurables.

00:07:05.961 --> 00:07:08.204
The steps in the Four Immeasurables.

00:07:08.204 --> 00:07:10.270
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD BDE BA THAMS CAD DANG

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:11.103
LDAN NA CI MA RUNG

00:07:11.103 --> 00:07:14.544
LDAN PAR GYUR CIG, LDAN
PAR BDAG GIS BYA'O,

00:07:14.544 --> 00:07:17.718
DE LTAR BYED NUS PAR BLA MA
LHAS BYIN GYIS BRLAB TU GSOL

00:07:17.718 --> 00:07:20.010
This is a very, very famous formula.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:24.951
May all the moms in my
world have happiness.

00:07:24.951 --> 00:07:26.360
Wouldn't that be nice?

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.884
CI MA RUNG means wouldn't that be nice?

00:07:28.884 --> 00:07:30.523
Wouldn't that be cool?

00:07:30.523 --> 00:07:34.769
LDAN PAR GYUR CIG -- Yeah!
They should have happiness.

00:07:34.769 --> 00:07:37.393
DE LTA BU DANG LDAN PA ZHIG BDAG GIS BYA'O

00:07:37.393 --> 00:07:40.769
I'll do it. I'll take care of
it. I'll take responsibility.

00:07:40.769 --> 00:07:42.640
So "wouldn't it be nice"

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:47.421
changes to "they should
have it", changes to

00:07:47.421 --> 00:07:50.560
"I'll be the one who makes sure they get".

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:53.410
So three steps here: CI MA RUNG

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:57.167
Hey, how nice it would be
if all my moms were happy?

00:07:57.167 --> 00:08:00.950
LDAN PAR GYUR CIG - Yeah, they
should. Let's make it happen.

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:02.810
I'll make it happen.

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:04.410
So those are the three steps.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:08.196
We can see three steps
here in the picture.

00:08:08.196 --> 00:08:12.210
Sometimes it takes me a
long time to find a picture.

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:15.880
Sometimes it just comes right away.

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:18.070
Yeah, three steps.

00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:19.667
So tell me the three.

00:08:19.667 --> 00:08:22.564
Number one. CI MA RUNG.

00:08:22.564 --> 00:08:26.860
Wouldn't that be nice if
all my moms could be happy?

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.010
Then GYUR CIG

00:08:28.010 --> 00:08:29.740
Yeah! That should happen.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:31.240
Step number two.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:34.630
Then step number three:
I'll make it happen.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:36.105
I'll take responsibility.

00:08:36.105 --> 00:08:38.490
By the way in the immeasurables,

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:41.902
there's a fourth step that
he doesn't mention here.

00:08:41.902 --> 00:08:44.620
DE LTAR BYED NUS PAR BLA MA
LHAS BYIN GYIS BRLAB TU GSOL

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.765
What does that mean?

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:51.090
Yeah. Hey Lama. Hey Teacher.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:55.328
Teacher, Lama and Angel, Lama-hla.

00:08:55.328 --> 00:08:57.370
Please, help me do it.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:00.982
He didn't have it here.

00:09:00.982 --> 00:09:03.860
DE LTAR BYAMS PA BSGOMS PA'I PHAN YON NI

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:08.050
So if you have this kind
of attraction to people,

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:10.806
love for people -- BSGOMS PA NI --

00:09:10.806 --> 00:09:13.810
what's going to happen to you,

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:16.440
if you reach a place in your life,

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:18.810
when you're looking at other people

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:22.359
and they just look beautiful
to you? What's the karma?

00:09:22.359 --> 00:09:24.840
What kind of karma is that?

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:28.210
What happens to you if
you have this karma?

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:33.210
RIN PHRENG LAS means
RIN CHEN PHRENG BA LAS

00:09:33.568 --> 00:09:38.568
It's ratna, not mala.

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:41.605
What's the other word for mala?

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:51.420
There's another Sanskrit
word for mala, for a garland.

00:09:52.116 --> 00:09:54.542
[Student] (unclear)

00:09:57.259 --> 00:09:58.937
ratna....

00:09:58.937 --> 00:10:00.612
You look it up.

00:10:00.612 --> 00:10:01.960
It has two names.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:05.108
Some people say ratna.

00:10:05.108 --> 00:10:09.016
And some people say, I forgot it.

00:10:10.525 --> 00:10:14.750
,RDZI 'U TSOS SUM BRGYA'I KHA ZAS DAG,

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.674
,NYIN RE DUS GSUM SBYIN PAS KYANG,

00:10:16.674 --> 00:10:18.557
,BYAMS PA YUD TZAM THANG GCIG GI,

00:10:18.557 --> 00:10:20.732
,BSOD NAMS DAG LA CHAR MI PHOD,

00:10:20.732 --> 00:10:23.070
There's a famous story

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:28.070
that you cook beautiful dishes for others,

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:33.814
especially for a group of monks or nuns.

00:10:33.814 --> 00:10:37.890
You cook for 300 of them every day,

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:42.530
and three times you give them
breakfast, lunch, and dinner.

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:44.113
So the idea is like, I don't know,

00:10:44.113 --> 00:10:45.663
you invite the Dalai Lama,

00:10:45.663 --> 00:10:49.310
you invite some holy being to your house

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:54.278
and you feed them 300 homemade dishes

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:59.650
three times in one day.

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:04.410
But even compared to
feeding these high lamas,

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:07.608
high nuns, high monks,

00:11:07.608 --> 00:11:12.608
BYAMS PA YUD TZAM means, if
you just have a passing moment

00:11:12.710 --> 00:11:14.880
in your life, where you're like,

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:17.790
"Oh, these people are so beautiful,"

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:21.892
if you just have that thought
just go through your mind

00:11:21.892 --> 00:11:23.920
one time like that,

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:26.150
"Oh, these people are so beautiful,"

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:30.900
it's more powerful than
serving thousands of meals

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:32.830
to very high lamas.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:35.200
It's more good karma

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:39.373
than feeding all these
meals to high lamas.

00:11:39.373 --> 00:11:40.963
BSOD NAMS DAG LA CHAR MI PHOD

00:11:40.963 --> 00:11:44.374
CHAR MI PHOD means you
can't compare the karma.

00:11:44.374 --> 00:11:48.114
CHAR MI PHOD means it doesn't make 1%.

00:11:48.114 --> 00:11:51.285
The karma of serving, of cooking,

00:11:51.285 --> 00:11:55.050
what do you call that, homemade meal

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:57.770
for a thousand high lamas

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:59.610
or just having a passing thought

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.240
"oh, these people around
me are so beautiful,"

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.220
I would like them to be happy.

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:08.157
That's better karma, more good karma.

00:12:08.157 --> 00:12:10.099
You got that?

00:12:13.193 --> 00:12:16.166
Come on, ratnamala.

00:12:16.166 --> 00:12:18.010
I'm going to tell you later.

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:21.133
You can find it.

00:12:21.133 --> 00:12:23.310
His book is not called Ratnamala,

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:26.518
it's called something else.

00:12:27.536 --> 00:12:30.141
[Student] (unclear)

00:12:30.141 --> 00:12:32.674
No, keep looking.

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:36.470
I'll look it up later.

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:41.021
Here's a verse. He's
going to quote a verse.

00:12:41.021 --> 00:12:43.479
,LHA MI BYAMS PAR 'GYUR BA DANG,

00:12:43.479 --> 00:12:45.750
this is what's going to happen

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:47.960
to you if you...

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:52.960
This is the power of the
karma, of sitting on a chair

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:57.550
and looking at other people and
feel like they're beautiful.

00:12:57.550 --> 00:13:02.550
They're like my own kid and,
"I would like you to be happy.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:05.284
You look so beautiful to me."

00:13:05.284 --> 00:13:09.350
LHA MI BYAMS PAR 'GYUR
BA, the LHAs and the MIs

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:12.208
will be BYAMS PA to you.

00:13:12.208 --> 00:13:14.721
What's that mean?

00:13:14.721 --> 00:13:19.579
The powerful gods, worldly gods,

00:13:19.579 --> 00:13:22.597
and also the tantric gods and humans,

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:25.320
they will like you.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:28.541
When you meet people, they'll
be friendly to you and say,

00:13:28.541 --> 00:13:29.724
"Hi, good morning."

00:13:29.724 --> 00:13:32.040
I went this morning for a
blood test, regular checkup.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:34.858
And the lady was so nice and she's just...

00:13:34.858 --> 00:13:37.660
Boy, she has to sit there all day,

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:41.850
get up at four o'clock, five
o'clock, and she was so nice.

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:43.720
And that's just BYAMS PA.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:46.522
People will be BYAMS PA to you.

00:13:46.522 --> 00:13:49.164
DE DAG KYANG NI SRUNG BA DANG

00:13:49.164 --> 00:13:52.364
They'll also take steps

00:13:52.364 --> 00:13:53.927
to make sure you're okay.

00:13:53.927 --> 00:13:55.076
They'll protect you,

00:13:55.076 --> 00:13:59.107
like Jigme came and picked me up early

00:13:59.107 --> 00:14:01.208
in the morning to go there.

00:14:01.208 --> 00:14:02.424
YID BDE BA DANG

00:14:02.424 --> 00:14:05.840
Then you'll always feel happy.

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:08.090
Deep down inside you'll feel happy.

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:12.372
This is from having those one
moments of vali, ratnavali.

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:20.720
YID BDE BA -- You'll feel happy

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:24.725
and BDE MANG means good
things will keep happening

00:14:24.725 --> 00:14:26.070
to you all through the day.

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:28.040
By the way, what's this karma?

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:29.830
Just for a few seconds

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:34.186
you think about how beautiful
people are around you.

00:14:34.186 --> 00:14:37.494
DUG DANG MTSON GYIS GNOD MED DANG

00:14:37.494 --> 00:14:41.330
You can eat some bad
Mexican food in America

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:44.430
and it won't make you sick.

00:14:44.430 --> 00:14:47.817
MTSON GYIS GNOD means people attack

00:14:47.817 --> 00:14:51.050
you with a gun or a knife

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:53.570
and nothing will happen to you.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:55.360
This is just from those moments

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:56.900
of thinking people are beautiful.

00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:59.550
This is the karma.

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:01.610
There's eight of the karmas.

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:03.759
He's listing eight.

00:15:03.759 --> 00:15:06.259
'BAD PA MED PAR DON 'THOB DANG

00:15:06.259 --> 00:15:08.890
Without trying very hard,

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:11.680
all the stuff you want to
happen in your life will happen.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:15.490
You will succeed in all
your projects and things

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:18.172
without much hard work.

00:15:18.172 --> 00:15:19.690
TSANGS PA'I 'JIG RTEN SKYE 'GYUR TE

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:23.420
You'll be born into the
world of the pure one,

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:27.198
which sometimes means a kind
of a temporary god heaven,

00:15:27.198 --> 00:15:30.810
and Brahma is the boss there.

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:35.448
But on a higher level, it
means a Buddha paradise.

00:15:35.448 --> 00:15:38.284
GAL TE GROL BAR MA GYUR KYANG

00:15:38.284 --> 00:15:42.080
Even if you don't get
enlightened right away,

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:47.179
just by those moments of
feeling love for people,

00:15:47.179 --> 00:15:48.812
BYAMS CHOS YON TAN BRGYAD 'THOB BO

00:15:48.812 --> 00:15:50.462
these eight wonderful things

00:15:50.462 --> 00:15:52.972
will be happening to you.

00:15:52.972 --> 00:15:55.347
ZHES GSUNGS PA LTAR, BYAMS CHOS
YON TAN BRGYAD 'THOB PA SOGS

00:15:55.347 --> 00:15:57.050
PHAN YON SHIN TU CHE'O

00:15:57.050 --> 00:16:02.050
Therefore, these eight
benefits of the karma,

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:05.740
of just seeing other people
as beautiful once in a while,

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:06.780
will come to you.

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:08.410
So that's a pretty easy way

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:13.350
to get a lot of beautiful
results is just to...

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.560
And normally, I mean,
I don't know about you.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:19.126
If you're not in a good mood,

00:16:19.126 --> 00:16:22.250
you're looking at people,
and driving your car,

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:23.470
and Geshe Michael's driving his car,

00:16:23.470 --> 00:16:26.090
and he's like irritated at everybody.

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:30.940
We're talking about catch your mind

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:33.904
when it's being irritated at people

00:16:33.904 --> 00:16:36.444
and then catch it and say, "Come on,

00:16:36.444 --> 00:16:38.968
how beautiful are people?

00:16:38.968 --> 00:16:40.267
people are beautiful."

00:16:40.267 --> 00:16:42.639
You want to live by yourself in a closet?

00:16:42.639 --> 00:16:45.580
It's not going to make you happy.

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:49.663
People are beautiful.
Go hang out with people.

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:55.620
Now, there's a very wonderful verse

00:16:56.900 --> 00:17:01.900
by Arya Nagarjuna that I
would like to include here.

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:07.330
So I'm inserting a new
verse into the text.

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:11.700
This is one of my favorite
verses of all time.

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:16.250
If I'm not mistaken,
it's also the Ratnavali.

00:17:17.418 --> 00:17:19.970
And I think, yeah.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:21.978
Anyway, here it is.

00:17:21.978 --> 00:17:24.792
I teach it to people in DCI a lot.

00:17:24.792 --> 00:17:27.066
And I'd like you guys to,

00:17:27.066 --> 00:17:29.316
I like to show it to you

00:17:29.316 --> 00:17:34.300
because it's talking about
the power of that karma

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:37.260
of just thinking that the
people around you are beautiful.

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:38.901
Just for a few minutes

00:17:38.901 --> 00:17:41.354
think of people around are beautiful.

00:17:41.354 --> 00:17:43.216
So let's go through this verse.

00:17:43.216 --> 00:17:48.216
You want to show this verse? Come on.

00:17:48.648 --> 00:17:50.940
You have the verse on Nagarjuna?

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:53.214
Okay here we go.

00:17:53.214 --> 00:17:55.410
I didn't put the pronunciation.

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:57.270
I didn't put the technical pronunciation

00:17:57.270 --> 00:17:59.410
but I'll do it with you here.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:01.452
Please say. You guys, ready?

00:18:01.452 --> 00:18:04.038
danad

00:18:04.038 --> 00:18:06.616
bhogah

00:18:06.616 --> 00:18:08.447
sukham

00:18:08.447 --> 00:18:10.432
shilat

00:18:10.432 --> 00:18:12.831
kshantyah

00:18:12.831 --> 00:18:14.893
kantih

00:18:14.893 --> 00:18:17.291
shramad

00:18:17.291 --> 00:18:19.379
dyutih

00:18:19.379 --> 00:18:21.725
dhyarach

00:18:21.725 --> 00:18:24.020
chantir

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:25.928
mater

00:18:25.928 --> 00:18:27.888
muktih

00:18:27.888 --> 00:18:29.951
kirpa

00:18:29.951 --> 00:18:32.892
sarvartha

00:18:32.892 --> 00:18:35.399
sadhani

00:18:35.399 --> 00:18:37.918
Okay, good. Let's go through it.

00:18:37.918 --> 00:18:41.500
These are the correlations,
karmic correlations

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:43.490
as presented by Nagarjuna,

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:47.231
extremely beautiful,

00:18:47.231 --> 00:18:51.381
extremely complete in a single verse.

00:18:51.381 --> 00:18:53.360
People tell me, "I want
to learn some Tibetan,

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:55.587
I want to learn some Sanskrit."

00:18:55.587 --> 00:18:56.744
Then learn this verse.

00:18:56.744 --> 00:18:59.195
This is a great verse to learn.

00:18:59.195 --> 00:19:03.230
It's very powerful to
have verses in your mind.

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:06.160
It's like having Nagarjuna
talk to you all day long.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:07.300
It's very beautiful.

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:11.910
So memorize it. Memorize it.

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:14.401
These are the karmic correlations

00:19:14.401 --> 00:19:16.439
according to Arya Nagarjuna.

00:19:16.439 --> 00:19:18.570
Danad bhogah

00:19:20.156 --> 00:19:23.152
Danad... Dana means what, you guys?

00:19:23.152 --> 00:19:25.980
Giving.

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:30.486
And then what's the long "a-t" in Sanskrit

00:19:30.486 --> 00:19:32.510
at the end of a word?

00:19:32.510 --> 00:19:35.826
Long "a-t"? Yeah, from.

00:19:35.826 --> 00:19:40.811
From doing danad you will get this.

00:19:40.811 --> 00:19:45.805
So he keeps repeating
this AT, which for an A,

00:19:45.805 --> 00:19:50.551
a noun ending in A, means from.

00:19:50.551 --> 00:19:52.195
Danad means from.

00:19:52.195 --> 00:19:55.153
And the T changes to D
before a B, that's all. BH.

00:19:55.153 --> 00:19:56.635
So danad.

00:19:56.635 --> 00:19:59.660
What do you get from
giving things to people?

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:02.217
Bhogah. Bhogah means?

00:20:02.217 --> 00:20:03.621
[Student] Enjoyment?

00:20:03.621 --> 00:20:05.579
Yeah, lots of stuff.

00:20:05.579 --> 00:20:08.220
Like sambhogakaya, right?

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:13.220
You get money. You're
going to get prosperous.

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:16.021
Your life is going to be full of

00:20:16.021 --> 00:20:19.712
money, houses, cars, things,

00:20:21.362 --> 00:20:24.140
beautiful things, nice
things, good things to have.

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:27.870
You can have more money
to help ALL, for example.

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:30.388
Just call the "Club de oro".

00:20:32.871 --> 00:20:37.871
But you get that money
to give to good charities

00:20:38.188 --> 00:20:39.638
by dana.

00:20:40.738 --> 00:20:43.380
Now because of poetry,

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:46.191
he has to say the next one backwards.

00:20:46.191 --> 00:20:50.716
Shilat from shila.

00:20:50.716 --> 00:20:53.440
Yeah, ethical lifestyle.

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:56.760
Literally shila means...
Do you know? Means what?

00:20:56.760 --> 00:21:01.022
Cool and refreshing. Shila.

00:21:01.022 --> 00:21:03.930
So shilat... From being
nice to other people

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:06.320
you get sukha.

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:08.540
You just feel happy all the time.

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:10.700
So by the way, by now

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:15.130
you can see that he's going
through the six perfections.

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:18.176
What's the next one that we expect?

00:21:18.176 --> 00:21:21.076
Yeah. Don't get upset.

00:21:21.076 --> 00:21:24.267
Kshantyah means patience.

00:21:24.267 --> 00:21:27.920
Kshanti means patience.

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:31.325
And this KSH in Sanskrit

00:21:31.325 --> 00:21:35.558
often changes to QUI in English.

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:38.696
So quiet,

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:42.913
like quiet from peacefulness.

00:21:42.913 --> 00:21:45.542
You get kantih.

00:21:45.542 --> 00:21:47.208
Kantih means golden.

00:21:47.208 --> 00:21:50.391
De oro... d'oro?

00:21:50.391 --> 00:21:51.225
That's kantih.

00:21:51.225 --> 00:21:56.225
It means golden complexion,
which means beauty,

00:21:56.650 --> 00:21:58.702
either handsome or beautiful.

00:21:58.702 --> 00:22:03.702
So either Pachi or Pau, you
can get from being patient,

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:05.987
in your past life.

00:22:05.987 --> 00:22:08.778
Next life, we don't know yet.

00:22:12.800 --> 00:22:16.170
So that means if you don't
get angry with people,

00:22:16.170 --> 00:22:19.886
then your face will become
more and more beautiful.

00:22:19.886 --> 00:22:22.570
He says golden.

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:24.757
Shramad dyutih.

00:22:24.757 --> 00:22:28.084
Sharamad means like shramanera.

00:22:28.084 --> 00:22:31.550
It means hard work.

00:22:31.550 --> 00:22:34.763
And it also has an implication of fun.

00:22:35.710 --> 00:22:38.118
If you have fun,

00:22:38.118 --> 00:22:41.984
BRTZON GANG DGE LA SPRO BA'O

00:22:41.984 --> 00:22:45.934
Shantideva defines the fourth perfection

00:22:45.934 --> 00:22:50.810
as having fun, when you're
doing good stuff for people.

00:22:50.810 --> 00:22:53.998
So just having fun, doing good things,

00:22:53.998 --> 00:22:56.011
not bad things.

00:22:56.011 --> 00:22:59.243
That's called the shrama.

00:23:00.501 --> 00:23:01.921
And shramad dyutih,

00:23:01.921 --> 00:23:04.045
dyutih is a very interesting word.

00:23:04.045 --> 00:23:06.984
It's the modern Hindi
word for electricity.

00:23:08.697 --> 00:23:13.580
Yeah, and it means you will
have an electric personality.

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:16.370
And it means you will become a leader.

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:18.200
People will be attracted to you.

00:23:18.200 --> 00:23:22.260
You will have a powerful,
attractive personality.

00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:25.521
What do you call that? You will be...

00:23:25.521 --> 00:23:26.384
[Student] Charismatic?

00:23:26.384 --> 00:23:27.799
[GMR] Charismatic, exactly.

00:23:27.799 --> 00:23:29.311
That's called dyutih.

00:23:29.311 --> 00:23:31.507
You will have an electric presence.

00:23:31.507 --> 00:23:35.565
It's also the word for
lightning in ancient Sanskrit.

00:23:37.335 --> 00:23:39.560
Dyutih

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:43.768
Dhyanach means... it's from dhyana,

00:23:43.768 --> 00:23:45.309
from meditation.

00:23:45.309 --> 00:23:48.610
Shanti

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:51.520
SHA changes to CHA after C.

00:23:51.520 --> 00:23:54.177
So this chantir is shanti,

00:23:54.177 --> 00:23:55.010
which means peaceful.

00:23:55.010 --> 00:23:56.950
You will always be peaceful.

00:23:56.950 --> 00:23:59.670
So he's going through the six perfections

00:23:59.670 --> 00:24:02.120
and he's doing the karmic correlations

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:05.010
in a single beautiful verse.

00:24:05.010 --> 00:24:07.160
And it's very good to memorize.

00:24:07.160 --> 00:24:09.220
If you want to know some Sanskrit,

00:24:09.220 --> 00:24:12.410
if you want to impress other
people at cocktail parties

00:24:12.410 --> 00:24:15.393
in Lake Chapala,

00:24:17.968 --> 00:24:19.701
around there and in those restaurants,

00:24:19.701 --> 00:24:23.603
then learn one verse of Sanskrit.

00:24:23.603 --> 00:24:28.603
Shanti. Mater means mati. Yeah, the mind,

00:24:28.603 --> 00:24:30.756
meaning

00:24:30.756 --> 00:24:32.850
you understand the two
husbands in the kitchen.

00:24:32.850 --> 00:24:35.135
That's called mati.

00:24:35.135 --> 00:24:37.443
And the ablative is mater,

00:24:37.443 --> 00:24:40.409
from mates,

00:24:40.409 --> 00:24:44.751
from understanding -- muktih,

00:24:44.751 --> 00:24:47.440
you get free.

00:24:47.440 --> 00:24:49.700
Yeah. You get freedom.

00:24:49.700 --> 00:24:52.250
Freedom comes from
understanding your husband

00:24:52.250 --> 00:24:56.720
in the kitchen when he yells at you.

00:24:56.720 --> 00:25:01.720
Now, Geshe-la, why did you
put this verse in here?

00:25:01.845 --> 00:25:03.780
We aren't talking about it.

00:25:03.780 --> 00:25:06.490
I mean, that's very sweet, but
we aren't talking about that.

00:25:06.490 --> 00:25:08.810
Yeah, but we're talking
about the next one,

00:25:08.810 --> 00:25:12.322
which is kirpa sarvartha sadhani.

00:25:12.322 --> 00:25:17.322
Kirpa means love.

00:25:17.367 --> 00:25:20.534
Kirpa means love.

00:25:22.277 --> 00:25:25.247
Sarva means all.

00:25:25.247 --> 00:25:28.423
Sarva atha means like Siddhartha, goals.

00:25:30.254 --> 00:25:34.120
Sadhani -- you will reach...

00:25:34.120 --> 00:25:36.024
This SADH means to reach.

00:25:36.024 --> 00:25:38.700
You will reach all your goals.

00:25:38.700 --> 00:25:43.440
What's he saying is that, and
that's very extraordinary.

00:25:43.440 --> 00:25:46.830
And I think a lot of my
Christian friends would agree.

00:25:46.830 --> 00:25:49.360
He says, Yeah, you can
practice those six perfections.

00:25:49.360 --> 00:25:50.760
Those are important.

00:25:50.760 --> 00:25:53.720
Each one has a powerful karmic result,

00:25:53.720 --> 00:25:57.230
and, of course, you should practice them.

00:25:57.230 --> 00:25:59.455
But actually, if you have five minutes

00:25:59.455 --> 00:26:03.037
of true love for somebody else,

00:26:03.037 --> 00:26:06.305
it achieves all those goals
together. All six goals.

00:26:08.667 --> 00:26:13.050
Sarvartha -- you get all six
goals together by having 5

00:26:13.050 --> 00:26:16.144
or 10 minutes of real
love for somebody else,

00:26:16.144 --> 00:26:18.540
beautiful love, beauty love, right?

00:26:18.540 --> 00:26:23.540
Cool? So don't forget that one.

00:26:23.800 --> 00:26:26.805
A passing moment where
you think all the people

00:26:26.805 --> 00:26:30.440
around you are super beautiful

00:26:30.440 --> 00:26:34.930
is equal to the karma of
those six perfections?

00:26:34.930 --> 00:26:36.093
Wow.

00:26:37.493 --> 00:26:39.667
Or feeding a million monks.

00:26:39.667 --> 00:26:40.853
All right.

00:26:42.078 --> 00:26:43.688
Next part of the text.

00:26:43.688 --> 00:26:47.410
BYAMS PA BSGOM PA 'DI'I DMIGS
YUL DU CI TZAM KHYAB PAS

00:26:47.410 --> 00:26:50.640
Now when you feel people are beautiful,

00:26:50.640 --> 00:26:54.050
the bigger you can make that feeling,

00:26:54.050 --> 00:26:56.930
the more you can multiply the karma.

00:26:56.930 --> 00:27:01.598
The more people you
feel beautiful love for,

00:27:01.598 --> 00:27:04.927
the more that love is powerful.

00:27:04.927 --> 00:27:06.235
KHYAB PAS

00:27:06.235 --> 00:27:09.110
DE TZAM LA DBANG BA'I 'KHOR BSGYUR DANG

00:27:09.110 --> 00:27:11.010
TSANGS PAR SKYE BAR 'GYUR

00:27:11.010 --> 00:27:15.150
If you can kind of stretch
it out to more people,

00:27:15.150 --> 00:27:18.462
the karma is that you will
become 'KHOR LO SGYUR BA,

00:27:18.462 --> 00:27:21.212
chakravartin, yeah.

00:27:22.520 --> 00:27:25.380
Wheel emperor, yeah. What's the wheel?

00:27:25.380 --> 00:27:27.440
A spaceship.

00:27:28.854 --> 00:27:31.556
It means King of the World.

00:27:31.556 --> 00:27:33.933
It's means President of the Whole World.

00:27:33.933 --> 00:27:35.270
So it's interesting.

00:27:35.270 --> 00:27:38.006
If you have these occasional feelings

00:27:38.006 --> 00:27:43.006
that people around you are
beautiful and you love them,

00:27:43.240 --> 00:27:45.980
that's a very powerful good karma.

00:27:45.980 --> 00:27:50.330
If you can just push it a little further

00:27:50.330 --> 00:27:54.390
towards more people, then it's
going to suddenly multiply

00:27:54.390 --> 00:27:57.630
and you will be King of the World.

00:27:57.630 --> 00:27:58.890
That's not much.

00:27:58.890 --> 00:28:00.742
Okay, 10 more people.

00:28:00.742 --> 00:28:03.231
- Hey, you want to be
king of the world? - Yeah.

00:28:03.231 --> 00:28:05.264
- Do you feel beautiful love for people?

00:28:05.264 --> 00:28:06.864
- Like a couple.

00:28:06.864 --> 00:28:08.960
- Can you just stretch
it to 10 more people?

00:28:08.960 --> 00:28:11.300
You can be King of the World if you do.

00:28:11.300 --> 00:28:13.783
- Okay. I'll do that.

00:28:13.783 --> 00:28:15.641
DE TZAM LA DBANG BA'I 'KHOR BSGYUR DANG

00:28:15.641 --> 00:28:16.791
TSANGS PAR SKYE BAR 'GYUR

00:28:16.791 --> 00:28:20.628
TSANGS PA means this very powerful

00:28:20.628 --> 00:28:22.870
worldly god, Brahma,

00:28:22.870 --> 00:28:27.378
who rules over entire realms of planets,

00:28:27.378 --> 00:28:30.053
a billion worlds.

00:28:30.053 --> 00:28:34.187
'DI LA TSANGS PA'I GNAS ZHES
BYA BA'ANG DE'I PHYIR YIN LA

00:28:34.187 --> 00:28:36.270
That's why the verse above said

00:28:36.270 --> 00:28:38.830
you can go to the place of Brahma

00:28:38.830 --> 00:28:42.036
if you have this beautiful love.

00:28:42.036 --> 00:28:44.094
NAM MKHA'I MTHA' KHYAB
KYI SEMS CAN THAMS CAD LA

00:28:44.094 --> 00:28:45.647
DMIGS PAS NI

00:28:45.647 --> 00:28:50.647
But if you can stretch that
beautiful love to all beings

00:28:50.647 --> 00:28:54.941
equal in extent to the universe itself,

00:28:54.941 --> 00:28:58.370
TSANGS PA CHEN PO MI GNAS PA'I MYANG 'DAS

00:28:58.370 --> 00:29:01.495
we call it the great brahma,

00:29:01.495 --> 00:29:05.877
maha brahma, meaning buddhahood.

00:29:05.877 --> 00:29:07.061
You can reach buddhahood.

00:29:07.061 --> 00:29:12.058
Just try to stretch your
beautiful love a little wider.

00:29:12.916 --> 00:29:15.820
All right.

00:29:15.820 --> 00:29:17.500
That brings us to...

00:29:17.500 --> 00:29:18.565
How many we've got?

00:29:18.565 --> 00:29:23.348
MAR SHES, DRIN DRAN, DRIN GZO,
YI 'ONG BYAMS PA, SNYING RJE

00:29:24.375 --> 00:29:27.518
Is it? Are we on five?

00:29:27.518 --> 00:29:31.791
MAR SHES, DRIN DRAN, DRIN GZO,
YI 'ONG BYAMS PA, SNYING RJE

00:29:31.791 --> 00:29:34.420
Yeah, we're on number five.

00:29:34.420 --> 00:29:35.826
SNYING RJE CHEN PO -- great compassion,

00:29:35.826 --> 00:29:38.938
maha karuna, here we go.

00:29:38.938 --> 00:29:40.671
LNGA PA SNYING RJE CHEN PO NI

00:29:40.671 --> 00:29:42.679
Let's go onto number five,

00:29:42.679 --> 00:29:47.126
step number five of the
seven cause and effect

00:29:47.126 --> 00:29:49.795
for getting bodhisattva vision.

00:29:49.795 --> 00:29:51.323
SNYING RJE CHEN PO NI What is it?

00:29:51.323 --> 00:29:52.839
What is great compassion?

00:29:52.839 --> 00:29:56.787
SANGS RGYAS KYI THUN MONG
MIN PA'I NYE RGYU GRUNG PO

00:29:56.787 --> 00:30:00.204
GRUNG PO means this is the real sharp

00:30:00.204 --> 00:30:02.520
and effective tool

00:30:02.520 --> 00:30:05.700
that can help you reach
enlightenment itself.

00:30:05.700 --> 00:30:07.940
So now we're talking about compassion.

00:30:07.940 --> 00:30:12.490
Generally, the difference
between compassion

00:30:12.490 --> 00:30:17.120
and... what you say...

00:30:17.120 --> 00:30:20.015
Well, you can say BYAMS PA means that

00:30:20.015 --> 00:30:22.706
you love people.

00:30:22.706 --> 00:30:25.500
You feel maitri, compassion,

00:30:25.500 --> 00:30:29.779
and then SNYING RJE means you want

00:30:29.779 --> 00:30:32.173
to help them escape their pain.

00:30:32.173 --> 00:30:35.160
So BYAMS PA is you want
them to have something nice,

00:30:35.160 --> 00:30:40.160
and SNYING RJE means you
want them to escape pain.

00:30:41.802 --> 00:30:43.963
And we're going to get to it
later, but there's a big debate

00:30:43.963 --> 00:30:47.900
about, some people say
BYAMS PA comes first.

00:30:47.900 --> 00:30:50.293
You know, first you have to love someone,

00:30:50.293 --> 00:30:52.215
like your own child

00:30:52.215 --> 00:30:56.490
and then you can want
to take their pain away.

00:30:56.490 --> 00:30:59.010
And some people say, no, no, no.

00:30:59.010 --> 00:31:02.510
If a child falls down off of a
bicycle and hurts themselves,

00:31:02.510 --> 00:31:04.290
you don't give them candy.

00:31:04.290 --> 00:31:08.360
You fix the pain first, and
then you give them love.

00:31:08.360 --> 00:31:11.470
So compassion and love.

00:31:11.470 --> 00:31:13.832
GRUNG PO ZHIG YIN LA,
RJE RIN PO CHES KYANG

00:31:13.832 --> 00:31:16.173
RJE RIN PO CHES -- Je Tsongkapa said,

00:31:16.173 --> 00:31:20.939
LAM RIM CHEN PO'I NANG BYANG
CHUB SEMS SBYONG GI RIM PA'I

00:31:20.939 --> 00:31:22.672
SA BCAD MDZAD PA NA

00:31:22.672 --> 00:31:25.290
When Tsongkapa outlines the steps

00:31:25.290 --> 00:31:30.290
for getting to bodhichitta
or the bodhisattva's vision,

00:31:30.520 --> 00:31:34.300
he said in his LAM RIM CHEN MO,

00:31:34.300 --> 00:31:36.100
in his great Lam Rim,

00:31:36.100 --> 00:31:40.884
SNYING RJE CHEN PO THEG CHEN
GYI LAM GYI RTZA BAR BSTAN

00:31:40.884 --> 00:31:45.870
He said the whole seven
steps turn on compassion.

00:31:45.870 --> 00:31:49.080
All seven steps turn on compassion.

00:31:49.080 --> 00:31:53.952
Compassion is the center
of the airplane prop.

00:31:53.952 --> 00:31:56.606
And everything turns on compassion.

00:31:56.606 --> 00:31:58.360
Je Tsongkapa describes that way.

00:31:58.360 --> 00:32:02.250
Yes, there are seven steps,
but number five is the one

00:32:02.250 --> 00:32:04.956
that everything turns around.

00:32:04.956 --> 00:32:07.167
He thought it was the most important one.

00:32:07.167 --> 00:32:10.394
RGYU 'BRAS GZHAN RNAMS DE'I
RGYU 'BRAS SU 'GRO TSUL

00:32:10.394 --> 00:32:13.770
When you describe the
others as cause and effect,

00:32:13.770 --> 00:32:15.210
you're really not talking

00:32:15.210 --> 00:32:17.550
about cause and effect of bodhichitta.

00:32:17.550 --> 00:32:21.650
You're talking about
compassion as cause and effect.

00:32:21.650 --> 00:32:26.648
The relationship of all
the other five steps

00:32:26.648 --> 00:32:29.440
is that they are either
causes of compassion

00:32:29.440 --> 00:32:31.230
or results of compassion.

00:32:31.230 --> 00:32:33.182
And that's why we call this thing

00:32:33.182 --> 00:32:36.440
the five cause and effect steps.

00:32:36.440 --> 00:32:39.240
It's not that bodhichitta is the effect.

00:32:39.240 --> 00:32:44.240
It's that everything is
defined relative to compassion.

00:32:44.470 --> 00:32:46.269
He thought it was that important.

00:32:46.269 --> 00:32:48.835
'GRO TSUL ZHES DMIGS KYIS BSAL TE

00:32:48.835 --> 00:32:53.119
DMIGS KYIS BSAL TE means he
gave a unique explanation.

00:32:53.119 --> 00:32:57.110
DMIGS BSAL means special or unique.

00:32:57.110 --> 00:32:59.423
It's a very important
word in the monastery

00:32:59.423 --> 00:33:03.023
because DMIGS BSAL means
you have a formal exception

00:33:03.023 --> 00:33:04.566
from the abbot.

00:33:04.566 --> 00:33:06.480
You don't have to wash dishes.

00:33:06.480 --> 00:33:08.946
You don't have to do farming.

00:33:08.946 --> 00:33:11.768
I got a DMIGS BSAL for farming

00:33:11.768 --> 00:33:13.780
because I was the accountant.

00:33:13.780 --> 00:33:17.448
So you know, they made
me farm for one day.

00:33:17.448 --> 00:33:19.923
This is standing on an ox,

00:33:19.923 --> 00:33:21.970
standing on the back of an ox.

00:33:21.970 --> 00:33:25.387
And I died after the
first day and they said,

00:33:25.387 --> 00:33:28.800
"You stick to accounting,
you have a DMIGS BSAL.

00:33:28.800 --> 00:33:31.930
You don't have to go
out to do the farming."

00:33:31.930 --> 00:33:33.803
So that's called DMIGS BSAL.

00:33:33.803 --> 00:33:36.811
Here, compassion is a DMIGS BSAL.

00:33:36.811 --> 00:33:39.661
Compassion is a special case.

00:33:39.661 --> 00:33:41.709
Everything turns around compassion,

00:33:41.709 --> 00:33:45.566
according to Tsonkgapa.

00:33:45.566 --> 00:33:49.000
I like this picture of kids
jumping into the water.

00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:50.802
We were discussing what
country it should be.

00:33:50.802 --> 00:33:53.835
We don't know yet.

00:33:55.685 --> 00:33:59.190
But it seems to me from compassion

00:33:59.190 --> 00:34:02.080
you can jump off into
BDAG GZHAN MNYAM BRJE.

00:34:02.080 --> 00:34:07.020
What is BDAG GZHAN MNYAM
BRJE? Equal and exchange.

00:34:07.020 --> 00:34:09.461
Equal and exchange.

00:34:09.461 --> 00:34:13.449
Equal means every living being
has a right to happiness,

00:34:13.449 --> 00:34:15.920
equal right.

00:34:15.920 --> 00:34:20.260
Exchange means, put
yourself in other's shoes

00:34:20.260 --> 00:34:25.260
and watch you and see how
hard you are on people.

00:34:25.920 --> 00:34:27.080
It's funny.

00:34:27.080 --> 00:34:30.795
It doesn't mean, I'm
going to pretend I'm Pau,

00:34:30.795 --> 00:34:32.459
and I'm going to be nice or something.

00:34:32.459 --> 00:34:34.972
It doesn't mean that. It
means I'm going to be Pau

00:34:34.972 --> 00:34:35.873
and look at Geshe Michael,

00:34:35.873 --> 00:34:38.931
and see how much trouble
is Geshe Michael for Pau.

00:34:38.931 --> 00:34:42.920
So you can do equal.

00:34:42.920 --> 00:34:46.710
I'm equal to you. We have
equal right to happiness.

00:34:46.710 --> 00:34:50.151
Why should Geshe-la send somebody else out

00:34:50.151 --> 00:34:51.410
to get a croissant?

00:34:51.410 --> 00:34:53.553
Why can't other people send Geshe-la out

00:34:53.553 --> 00:34:54.476
to get a croissant?

00:34:54.476 --> 00:34:56.118
That would be equal, right.

00:34:56.118 --> 00:35:00.051
And then, how does it
feel when Geshe-la says,

00:35:00.051 --> 00:35:02.194
"You go get me a croissant",
but Geshe-la doesn't say,

00:35:02.194 --> 00:35:03.929
"I'll go get you a croissant?"

00:35:03.929 --> 00:35:07.373
It feels unfair. It feels unequal, right?

00:35:07.373 --> 00:35:11.050
So this is the two steps of MNYAM BRJE.

00:35:11.050 --> 00:35:16.050
If you can empathize
with other people's pain,

00:35:17.320 --> 00:35:20.270
then you can exchange
yourself with others.

00:35:20.270 --> 00:35:22.780
If you can be aware

00:35:22.780 --> 00:35:27.358
that someone else feels bad
about croissant running,

00:35:28.730 --> 00:35:33.550
if you reach that kind of
awareness or sensitivity

00:35:33.550 --> 00:35:36.833
to other people's feelings,
then you can exchange,

00:35:36.833 --> 00:35:37.675
then you can exchange.

00:35:37.675 --> 00:35:39.760
So this is a good place to jump off.

00:35:39.760 --> 00:35:43.500
If you want to do the other great method

00:35:43.500 --> 00:35:48.220
of getting to bodhichitta,
which is two steps:

00:35:48.220 --> 00:35:50.530
see that you're equal to others

00:35:50.530 --> 00:35:54.872
and then put yourself in
their eyes and look at you.

00:35:54.872 --> 00:35:58.550
That's the second classical
way to get bodhichitta.

00:35:58.550 --> 00:36:03.547
And this is a good place to
jump off from the five steps

00:36:05.900 --> 00:36:09.508
to jump to the two steps of Shantideva.

00:36:09.508 --> 00:36:11.244
This is a good place to jump.

00:36:11.244 --> 00:36:16.244
If you feel like there's a
special meditation practice,

00:36:16.910 --> 00:36:20.303
called, what is that called?

00:36:20.303 --> 00:36:23.619
I forgot.

00:36:23.619 --> 00:36:25.398
[Student] Exchange yourself and others?

00:36:25.398 --> 00:36:27.724
[GMR] No, this is like... you go up

00:36:27.724 --> 00:36:30.779
through the eight form realm levels

00:36:30.779 --> 00:36:32.506
and then you go up to
the eight, the four...

00:36:32.506 --> 00:36:34.932
Sorry, four and four.

00:36:34.932 --> 00:36:37.290
It's called %SPEL SGOM.

00:36:37.290 --> 00:36:39.340
%SPEL SGOM means you don't go

00:36:39.340 --> 00:36:42.038
one, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

00:36:42.038 --> 00:36:45.170
You go one, three, five, seven, six, four

00:36:45.170 --> 00:36:46.646
and you jump around.

00:36:46.646 --> 00:36:48.084
So if you feel like it,

00:36:48.084 --> 00:36:50.710
this is Geshe Michael giving
you an extra assignment.

00:36:50.710 --> 00:36:52.940
It's not in the text.

00:36:52.940 --> 00:36:54.730
If you want to get fancy

00:36:54.730 --> 00:36:58.260
and you want to challenge yourself,

00:36:58.260 --> 00:37:00.360
try to jump between the two methods

00:37:00.360 --> 00:37:02.630
of getting to bodhichitta.

00:37:02.630 --> 00:37:06.495
The first is the five steps
that we've been studying.

00:37:06.495 --> 00:37:09.524
And the second is BDAG GZHAN MNYAM BRJE.

00:37:09.524 --> 00:37:14.524
Equal, equal, become aware
that you are equal to others

00:37:14.730 --> 00:37:17.940
and then try to see how they see you.

00:37:17.940 --> 00:37:20.750
Which is called exchanging
self and others.

00:37:20.750 --> 00:37:22.030
But it's not what you think.

00:37:22.030 --> 00:37:23.940
It's not like put yourself in other shoes.

00:37:23.940 --> 00:37:25.770
It doesn't mean that.

00:37:25.770 --> 00:37:29.280
It means put yourself in Christina's body

00:37:29.280 --> 00:37:31.050
and look at Geshe Michael

00:37:31.050 --> 00:37:33.223
and see how it feels to be Christina.

00:37:34.110 --> 00:37:36.770
How is Geshe Michael treating Christina?

00:37:36.770 --> 00:37:40.030
See how it feels to Christina
to look at Geshe Michael

00:37:40.030 --> 00:37:42.972
and see how he treats her.

00:37:42.972 --> 00:37:44.860
So you can get a bodhichitta either way.

00:37:44.860 --> 00:37:49.151
What I'm saying is, Tsongkapa said,

00:37:49.151 --> 00:37:51.810
the five steps for getting

00:37:51.810 --> 00:37:56.360
to bodhichitta, they turn
around step number five...

00:37:56.360 --> 00:37:59.650
Sorry, the seven steps, turn
around step number five.

00:37:59.650 --> 00:38:03.520
And I'm saying another cool
thing is, if you want to,

00:38:03.520 --> 00:38:06.840
you can jump from step
five to Shantideva's way

00:38:06.840 --> 00:38:07.673
of getting bodhichitta.

00:38:07.673 --> 00:38:09.993
Right now we studying Atisha's way

00:38:09.993 --> 00:38:12.080
of getting bodhichitta, right?

00:38:12.080 --> 00:38:14.482
All right, here we go.

00:38:14.482 --> 00:38:18.857
MDO LAS KYANG, 'KHOR
BSGYUR GYI 'KHOR LO DANG,

00:38:18.857 --> 00:38:22.290
MI'I SROG GI DBANG PO LTAR
THEG CHEN GYI LAM 'BRAS BU DANG

00:38:22.290 --> 00:38:23.740
BCAS PA THAMS CAD KYANG

00:38:23.740 --> 00:38:26.050
'DI LA RAG LAS PAR GSUNGS SHING,

00:38:26.050 --> 00:38:28.790
If you are a wheel emperor or a...

00:38:28.790 --> 00:38:32.070
what do you call a flying saucer king?

00:38:32.070 --> 00:38:34.930
You need your flying saucer.

00:38:34.930 --> 00:38:38.839
If you're a bodhisattva,
you need your compassion.

00:38:38.839 --> 00:38:43.385
What he says here is
'KHOR BSGYUR GYI 'KHOR LO

00:38:43.385 --> 00:38:46.398
If you're going to be a spaceship king

00:38:46.398 --> 00:38:48.729
you better get a spaceship.

00:38:48.729 --> 00:38:50.059
If you're going to be a bodhisattva,

00:38:50.059 --> 00:38:52.852
you better get some compassion.

00:38:52.852 --> 00:38:57.852
Or if you want to be a living human being,

00:38:58.185 --> 00:39:00.870
and not a stone or a tree,

00:39:00.870 --> 00:39:05.200
you better have some life,
human life inside your body.

00:39:05.200 --> 00:39:10.200
So what he's saying is, in
the way that life animates

00:39:10.500 --> 00:39:15.500
the human body, compassion
animates the human soul.

00:39:18.589 --> 00:39:22.070
All right, 'DI LA RAG LAS PAR GSUNGS SHING

00:39:22.070 --> 00:39:24.710
Cool, we finished this class

00:39:24.710 --> 00:39:28.290
and then we're going to go on to...

00:39:28.290 --> 00:39:31.180
We're going to take a trip to Tsongkapa's

00:39:31.180 --> 00:39:34.680
greatest book on emptiness
because there's something there

00:39:34.680 --> 00:39:38.296
that's going to help us
with our bodhichitta.

00:39:38.296 --> 00:39:40.719
See you in the next class. Yay!

